{"results":[{"url":"https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/dhruv-tara-chs-borivali/103789/project","title":"Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali, Borivali East, Mumbai - Price on Request","raw_content":"# Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali Borivali East, Mumbai\n\n**Price on Request**\n\n## About Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali, Borivali East by\n\n## Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali Price List, Price Trends and Market Insights\n\n### Price List\n\nView the latest price list for Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali.\n\n| Unit Type (Carpet) | Price\\* | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 BHK Apartment  650 Sq. Ft. | **Price on Request** | Check Availability |\n\n\\*Prices are indicative and subject to applicable charges and project terms.\n\n### Price Trends\n\nDhruv Tara CHS Borivali's average asking price is stable quarter-on-quarter, compared with Borivali East.\n\nSep 2025 — Jun 2026\n\n| Quarter | Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali | Borivali East |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Jun 2026 | 23900 | 35650 |\n| Mar 2026 | 23900 | 34750 |\n| Dec 2025 | 24250 | 32450 |\n| Sep 2025 | 22350 | 30650 |\n\n### Comparable Projects\n\nDhruv Tara CHS Borivali avg. price is ₹ 23.9 K/Sq.Ft. compared to Borivali East at ₹ 35.6 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Project | Avg. ₹/sq ft |\n| --- | --- |\n| Borivali East | ₹ 35,650 |\n| [Chandak Nishchay](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/chandak-nishchay/10108/project \"Chandak Nishchay\") | ₹ 26,850 |\n| [Shapoorji Pallonji Sarova](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/shapoorji-pallonji-sarova/10427/project \"Shapoorji Pallonji Sarova\") | ₹ 26,250 |\n| Current Project **Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali** | ₹ 23,900 |\n| [Shapoorji Pallonji Sarova Complex](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/shapoorji-pallonji-sarova-complex/119475/project \"Shapoorji Pallonji Sarova Complex\") | ₹ 21,800 |\n\n### Rentals\n\nMonthly Rent in Borivali East ranges from ₹ 19.1 K to ₹ 1.5 L with options available for STUDIO,1,2,3,4 BHK units\n\n| Configuration | In Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali | In Borivali East |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 BHK | - | ₹ 31.8 K |\n| 2 BHK | - | ₹ 46.2 K |\n| 3 BHK | - | ₹ 98.6 K |\n| 4 BHK | - | ₹ 1.5 L |\n\n### Recent Updates\n\nGet the latest price and market updates for Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali.\n\n#### MMRDA Plans Two New Ring Roads to Ease Mumbai Traffic\n\nThe Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA) is planning two additional ring routes, expanding its proposed network from seven to nine. These new corridors will cover approximately 307 km and will connect existing roads and planned projects across Mumbai, Thane, and Navi Mumbai.\n\n#### Thane Infrastructure and Development Updates\n\nThe Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel project saw the launch of TBM Arjuna on August 13, 2026, aiming to reduce travel time between Thane and Borivali to approximately 15 minutes. Amazon Data Services is developing a large data center in Ambernath, with an estimated construction cost of ₹3,500 crore, to be ready by 2029\n\n#### Mumbai Boosts Connectivity with Santacruz - Chembur link road Phase 2 & Chembur Metro Station\n\nCM Devendra Fadnavis inaugurated Phase 2 of the Santacruz-Chembur Link Road (SCLR) & the Chembur Metro Station under Metro Line 2B,The SCLR Phase 2 is expected to strengthen the road network between Mumbai's western and eastern suburbs, improving east-west connectivity.\n\n#### Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel Project: Traffic Diversions Announced in Kasarvadavali\n\nTemporary traffic diversions have been implemented in Kasarvadavali for the ongoing work on the ambitious Thane-Borivali twin tunnel project by the Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA). Certain routes will be closed from July 6 to August 5, 2026, to facilitate construction.\n\n#### Mumbai Monorail Services to Resume After Nine-Month Hiatus\n\nMumbai's monorail services are set to resume soon after a nine-month suspension, following approval from the Maharashtra government for safety improvements and fare revisions. MMRDA has proposed increased ticket prices. The monorail, which previously carried around 18,000 passengers daily, will offer improved services after safety upgrades.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### MMRDA to Launch Metro Lines 2B and 9, Bhoomipujan for Thane-Borivali Tunnel and BKC Pod Taxi on April 7\n\nThe Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA) will inaugurate Metro Line 2B (Phase I) and Metro Line 9 (Phase I), and conduct the bhoomipujan for the Thane–Borivali Twin Tunnel project and the pod taxi system in Bandra Kurla Complex (BKC) on April 7. These projects aim to significantly reduce travel time, ease congestion, and improve connectivity across Mumbai's suburbs.\n\n#### Mumbai Local Trains Face Cancellations for Infrastructure Upgrade\n\nWestern Railway is undertaking essential infrastructure upgrades between Kandivali and Borivali from December 21, 2025, to January 18, 2026, leading to the daily cancellation of over 80 local trains. This includes work on tracks and crossovers, impacting suburban, passenger, and express train services. Nightly mega blocks are also in effect, causing further service disruptions.\n\nDuring Q4'2025, average property prices for Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali moved from ₹ 22,350/sqft to ₹ 24,250/sqft, reflecting a 8.50% rise.\n\n## Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali Floor Plans\n\n### 2 BHK 650 Sq. Ft. Apartment\n\n(Carpet Area)\n\nPrice: **Price on Request**\n\n## Amenities & Specifications of Dhruv Tara CHS Borivali\n\n### Sports Sports\n\n![Sports](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/sports/am-ico-kidsplay-active.svg)\n\n### Convenience Convenience\n\n![Convenience](https://s